# ⚠️  RENDER DOES NOT READ THIS FILE.
#
# `_redirects` is a Netlify / Cloudflare Pages convention. Render takes rewrite config from
# render.yaml (the HolDEX-frontend service's `routes:` block) or the Dashboard. Verified in
# production: /trenches/deep-link returned 404 rather than the SPA, so this rule was inert.
# /trenches/ itself only worked because a directory path serves index.html by default.
#
# EDITING THIS FILE ALONE CHANGES NOTHING - make the same edit in render.yaml.

# Render static-site rewrites. Files that actually exist are served before any rule here
# applies, so /trenches/assets/* and the site's own pages are unaffected.

# Trenches SPA: hand any /trenches/* URL back to the app's entry document so a refresh or a
# pasted link lands in the app instead of a 404. Status 200 = rewrite (URL stays put), not a
# redirect. The app keeps its tab state client-side rather than in the URL, so this is a
# safety net rather than routing.
/trenches/*  /trenches/index.html  200
